      "created_at": "2021-05-31T02:25:06.486Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Had a situation in one of the threads where I get a message when trying to post a short response that other folks aren’t getting. Is there a default setting on permissions that was changed for most users but left as-is for Mods, <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/cajunjoel\">@cajunjoel</a>? Copied from <a href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/t/question-of-the-day/15922/910\">the original</a>:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\" data-post=\"910\" data-topic=\"15922\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/7330_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"><a href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/t/question-of-the-day/15922/910\">Question of the Day!</a></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>When I post just \"ALL THE WOOD!!! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> \", I get an error saying “Body seems unclear, is it a complete sentence?” My bet is there’s a setting that the Admins changed for the default users that wasn’t changed for Mods, so I’ll pursue that with them. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-05-31T02:25:20.781Z",
